  "name": "The Larder",
  "id_prefix": "l1",
  "note": "Hand-made on-ramp (docs/plan-v2.md step 1). Each pack of 10 teaches one thing. L1-10 basics: everyday categories (tier 1, tier 2 from L4; the L10 hard level is all tier 2), no herrings, no lateral groups. L11-20 develop: slip limit from L11 (never below 3), Complete at L13, lateral groups ('Words after X') arrive on the L16 rest level, then on L18 and L20. L21-30 twist: herrings arrive on the L21 rest level, 4 groups on L26. Room 2 (L31-60) has a lateral group in nearly every level and herrings from L37, so both are taught before it. Every level is familiar (no hard words) and strict (no two cards of different groups share another bank category). Sawtooth per 10: 1-4 rise, 5 tricky, 6 rest (new idea), 7-9 rise, 10 hard; targets end just under Room 2's (0.8 normal, 1.4 hard).",
  "avoid_cats_note": "Categories too vague or niche for a first room: Kinds of poem draws Epic and Rhyme, which name no poem form a new player knows; Kinds of water draws Salt and Tonic and sits beside Ways water moves; the phonetic alphabet and snooker words are specialist knowledge (and Break and Spin read as dance moves).",
  "avoid_cats": ["kinds_of_poem", "kinds_of_water", "phonetic_alphabet", "snooker_words"],
  "avoid_words_note": "Words that read as another group's, or name their own weakly (from two reviews, one fresh-eyes). Cross-reads: Orchard and Meadow (trees, fields), Hoot, Howl, Roar and Snort (animal sounds), Mole (an animal), Glasses (a container), Swallow (a bird), Tumbler (a gymnast), Channel (TV), Dip (food), Forum (online), Engine and Helmet (space), Water (something that runs), Bakery (cakes), Present (time), Gill (pond life), Setting (on a screen), Balcony (a concert hall), Ink (writers), Brush (art), Chlorine (pools and bleach). Weak members: Beam, Stand, Fan, Display, Hook, Quarter, Atlas, Starch, Turn, Base, Tail, Fine, Leaf (of a flower), Tutor (household staff), Shrug and Upset (gym and sports senses), Chase (a game), Spell (magic), Cone, Needle and Sap (pine parts, not what players expect of a tree). Rare or regional: Newton, Dirham, Frappe, Jaggery, Canteen (a flask), Ottoman, Prairie.",
  "avoid_words": ["Orchard", "Meadow", "Hoot", "Howl", "Roar", "Snort", "Mole", "Glasses", "Swallow", "Tumbler", "Channel", "Dip",
    "Forum", "Engine", "Helmet", "Water", "Beam", "Stand", "Fan", "Display", "Hook", "Quarter", "Atlas", "Starch", "Turn", "Base",
